---
// Privacy policy (EN mirror of /datenschutz.html — same slug so the language
// switcher pairs the pages). Describes factually what this static site does.
// [TODO] fields must be filled before publishing.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
import Attribution from '../components/Attribution.astro';
---
<Layout title={"Privacy Policy | VerseBase"} description={"Privacy policy of VerseBase: what data is processed when visiting, by the cookieless reach measurement, when external images load, and when YouTube videos are clicked — including a one-click opt-out."} themeColor="#05070d" translated={true}>
<style is:inline>
:root{--bg:#05070d;--bg-2:#0a0e18;--surface:#0f1524;--surface-2:#141c30;--accent:#2dd4ff;--accent-2:#6ea8ff;--text:#e8eefc;--muted:#8a99b8;--line:rgba(110,168,255,.16);--line-soft:rgba(232,238,252,.10);--ink:#05070d;--maxw:840px;}
/* ⚠⚠ GESEHEN 30.08.2026 im Kontaktbogen: diese Seite rendert komplett in
   TIMES NEW ROMAN — Ueberschrift, Fliesstext, alles. Nachgemessen:
   getComputedStyle(body).fontFamily = "Times New Roman" auf
   /impressum, /datenschutz und beiden DE-Fassungen.
   Ursache: die Schrift-Token stehen NICHT global, sondern in den
   Seiten-Stylesheets (archive.css, data-page.css, account-dossier.css)
   bzw. bei eigenstaendigen Seiten in deren eigenem :root — siehe
   src/pages/404.astro Zeile 21. Diese Seite laedt keins davon und setzte
   sie auch nicht selbst, also lief jedes var(--font-…) ins Leere und
   der Browser nahm seinen Standard. Die Farbtokens kamen aus theme.css,
   deshalb sah die Seite auf den ersten Blick richtig aus.
   Dieselbe Zeile wie in 404.astro, damit beide dasselbe meinen. */
:root{--font-display:'Orbitron',sans-serif;--font-ui:'Rajdhani',sans-serif;--font-body:'Barlow',system-ui,sans-serif;--font-mono:'Share Tech Mono',monospace}
body{font-family:var(--font-body)}
/* Hellmodus — erzeugt von scripts/build-light-palettes.mjs. Nicht von Hand ändern. */
:root[data-theme="light"]{--bg:#f4f7fe;--bg-2:#e9eef9;--surface:#fdfdff;--surface-2:#eef2fc;--text:#1b1f29;--muted:#4e586c;--accent:#05657c;--accent-2:#0850ad;--ink:#ffffff;--accent-media:#2dd4ff;--accent-2-media:#6ea8ff;--line:rgba(43,125,148,.3);--line-soft:rgba(41,46,56,.12)}




/* ⚠ Gemessen 30.08.2026 (Tiefenpruefung): 3,2rem Polsterung = 57,6 px, die
   feste Kopfleiste ist aber 61 px (Schreibtisch), 69 px (Telefon) und
   86 px bei 768 px Breite hoch — mit Zurück-Zeile. Die Überschrift stand
   dadurch bei 768×1024 zwanzig Pixel HINTER der Leiste. --nav-h veröffentlicht
   SiteNav; der Rückfallwert deckt den Fall ohne SiteNav ab. */
.lg-wrap{max-width:var(--maxw);margin:0 auto;padding:calc(var(--nav-h, 69px) + 2.4rem) 1.25rem 4rem}
/* ⚠ GEMESSEN 31.08.2026: „Datenschutzerklärung" braucht bei dieser Größe
   456 px und hatte auf einem 360-px-Gerät 299 — der Browser brach mitten
   im Wort um („Datenschutze / rklärung"). Silbentrennung statt harter
   Schnitt: die Seite trägt lang="de", der Browser kennt die deutschen
   Trennmuster und setzt „Datenschutz- / erklärung". Die englische Fassung
   („Privacy Policy") ist kurz genug und bleibt unberührt — aber die Regel
   steht in beiden Sprachfassungen, damit sie nicht auseinanderlaufen. */
.lg-wrap h1{font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:900;font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,3rem);color:var(--text);margin:0 0 1.6rem;hyphens:auto;-webkit-hyphens:auto}
.lg-wrap h2{font-family:var(--font-ui);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:var(--ls-10);text-transform:uppercase;font-size:var(--fs-9);color:var(--accent);margin:2.2rem 0 .6rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding-bottom:.4rem}
.lg-wrap p, .lg-wrap li{color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;font-size:var(--fs-10)}
.lg-wrap ul{padding-left:1.2rem}
.lg-wrap .muted{color:var(--muted)}
.lg-wrap .optout{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.75rem;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem;margin:1.1rem 0;scroll-margin-top:6rem}
.lg-wrap .optout button{font:inherit;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;color:var(--ink);background:var(--accent);border:0;border-radius:6px;padding:.5rem .95rem}
.lg-wrap .optout button:hover{filter:brightness(1.08)}
.lg-wrap .optout .note{flex:1 1 100%;margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--fs-7);line-height:1.55}
.lg-wrap .optout code{font-size:.85em;color:var(--accent-2)}
.lg-fill{display:inline-block;background:color-mix(in srgb,#ff5b5b 14%,transparent);border:1px dashed #ff5b5b;border-radius:4px;padding:0 .45rem;color:#ffb4b4;font-weight:700}
/* Hell-Entsprechungen — erzeugt von scripts/build-light-overrides.mjs. Nicht von Hand ändern. */
:root[data-theme="light"] .lg-fill{color:#893c40}
</style>
<SiteNav crumbs={[{ label: 'Archive', href: '/archiv.html' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} hasEn={true} />
<main id="main">
  <div class="lg-wrap">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>
      Krisztofer Milánkovits, Schlossstraße 6, 85411 Hohenkammer, Germany —
      e-mail: <a href="mailto:krysx141@gmail.com">krysx141@gmail.com</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Principle</h2>
    <p>
      This website is a purely static, non-commercial fan project. It shows no advertising and
      has no comment functions. Reach is measured by two cookieless services:
      <a href="#cloudflare">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a> and the self-hosted
      <a href="#umami">Umami</a> — both without fingerprinting, without personal profiles and
      without storing anything on your device. You can <a href="#opt-out">opt out</a> with one
      click; only then is a technical
      cookie set, which records exactly that choice. Beyond that you only transmit
      data via the
      <a href="#feedback">feedback form</a> and the optional <a href="#accounts">user account</a> —
      both voluntary; the data processed there is described separately below.
    </p>

    <h2>Server log files (hosting)</h2>
    <p>
      When you visit this website, the hosting provider
      Hetzner Online GmbH (Industriestr. 25, 91710 Gunzenhausen, Germany) technically
      processes connection data (IP address, timestamp, requested resource, user agent) in server
      logs. Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure operation).
    </p>

    <h2 id="cloudflare">Delivery and reach measurement (Cloudflare)</h2>
    <p>
      The site is delivered via Cloudflare (Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend Street, San Francisco,
      CA 94107, USA). Cloudflare sits in front of the hosting as a proxy: every request passes
      through it, and connection data (IP address, timestamp, requested resource, user agent) is
      processed there for delivery and to fend off attacks.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare additionally adds <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> to the pages, a
      measurement script that records page views, visits and load times. It sets
      <strong>no cookies</strong>, uses no fingerprinting and does not follow you across other
      websites; we only ever see aggregated figures, never individual profiles. Legal basis:
      Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure, fast delivery and in basic reach
      figures). Processing on servers outside the EU is possible; for details see the provider's
      privacy policy:
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 id="umami">Self-hosted reach measurement (Umami)</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Umami</strong> also runs at stats.verse-base.com — open-source analytics operating
      on our own server. Recorded are the page visited, the referrer, country, device type,
      browser and operating system, plus time on page. <strong>No cookies are set and nothing is
      stored on your device</strong>; to tell visits apart, a checksum that changes daily is used,
      which cannot be traced back to anyone. The data never leaves our server — no third party is
      involved. Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (legitimate interest in reach figures). Your
      <a href="#opt-out">opt-out</a> stops this measurement too.
    </p>

    <div class="optout" id="opt-out">
      <span id="rum-status">Checking …</span>
      <button type="button" id="rum-toggle">Don't count me</button>
      <p class="note">
        Your choice is remembered by the technical cookie <code>vb_noanalytics</code> in this
        browser; its entire content is a 1 or a 0. It takes effect from the next page load and
        covers both services: the server then no longer allows the measurement scripts, so they
        never load at all. If you clear your cookies, you have to
        opt out here again. Whoever maintains the site is not counted while signed in anyway.
      </p>
    </div>
    <script is:inline>
      (() => {
        const NAME = 'vb_noanalytics';
        const off = () => document.cookie.split('; ').some((c) => c === NAME + '=1');
        const status = document.getElementById('rum-status');
        const btn = document.getElementById('rum-toggle');
        if (!status || !btn) return;
        const render = (hint) => {
          status.textContent = (off()
            ? 'You are not being counted here.'
            : 'You are currently being counted here.') + (hint ? ' ' + hint : '');
          btn.textContent = off() ? 'Count me again' : "Don't count me";
        };
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          document.cookie = (off()
            ? NAME + '=0'
            : NAME + '=1') + '; Max-Age=34560000; Path=/; SameSite=Lax; Secure';
          render('Applies from the next page load.');
        });
        render();
      })();
    </script>

    <h2>Local browser storage (localStorage)</h2>
    <p>
      Some tools on this site (e.g. the crafting planner, “owned” marks, view settings) store their
      state <strong>locally in your browser</strong> (localStorage). This data never
      leaves your device and can be deleted at any time via your browser settings. When you are
      signed in, the contents of account-bound tools (crafting planner and “owned” marks, refinery
      jobs) are additionally stored in your <a href="#accounts">user account</a> so they are
      available across devices.
    </p>

    <h2>Externally embedded images</h2>
    <p>
      Some imagery is loaded from external sources. When these images are fetched, your IP address
      is technically transmitted to the respective provider:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>fleetyards.net</strong> — ship and vehicle imagery</li>
      <li><strong>starcitizen.tools / cstone.space</strong> — individual media assets</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Ambient background videos</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages show short, muted video loops (trailer excerpts) as backgrounds. These files
      are served <strong>locally by this website</strong> — no third-party server is contacted.
      With reduced motion enabled (prefers-reduced-motion), an active data-saver mode, or on
      small screens, only the still image is loaded instead.
    </p>

    <h2>YouTube videos (click to load)</h2>
    <p>
      Videos are embedded as preview stills and load <strong>only after you click</strong>, via
      youtube-nocookie.com (Google Ireland Ltd.). Before the click, no connection to Google is made;
      after the click, <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy</a> applies.
    </p>

    <h2 id="feedback">Feedback form (Web3Forms)</h2>
    <p>
      On the <a href="/feedback.html">Feedback</a> page you can voluntarily send us a message.
      Because this website is static and has no server backend of its own, delivery is handled by the
      service <strong>Web3Forms</strong>. When you submit, the following data is transmitted to
      Web3Forms and delivered from there to us by e-mail:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>message text</strong> (required)</li>
      <li><strong>rating</strong> (1–5 stars, optional)</li>
      <li><strong>e-mail address</strong> (optional — only if you want a reply; it is set as the
        reply-to address)</li>
      <li>technically, your IP address and the time of submission</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The legal basis is your consent given by actively submitting the form (Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR).
      Providing your e-mail address is voluntary; without it we cannot reply to your feedback. We use
      the data solely to process and answer your feedback and do not pass it on for other purposes.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      The form service is provided by Web3Forms. Transmission may involve processing on servers
      outside the EU. For details on how the service processes data, see its privacy policy:
      <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" rel="noopener">web3forms.com/privacy</a>. The form sets
      no cookies and loads no external scripts; a connection to Web3Forms is only established upon
      submission.
    </p>

    <h2 id="accounts">User account (Supabase)</h2>
    <p>
      You can voluntarily create a user account to save favorites (e.g. bookmarked ships) and manage
      a profile. The account feature is provided via <strong>Supabase</strong>; the data is stored in
      an EU data center (AWS Frankfurt, region eu-central-1). The following data is processed:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>e-mail address</strong> and <strong>password</strong> (the password is stored
        exclusively as a cryptographic hash, never in plain text)</li>
      <li><strong>profile data</strong> you enter yourself (display name, handle — both optional)</li>
      <li><strong>favorites</strong> you actively save</li>
      <li><strong>tool data</strong> you actively create (crafting planner and “owned” marks,
        refinery jobs)</li>
      <li>technically, session and security data of the provider (e.g. sign-in timestamps,
        IP address in security logs)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR (providing the account feature at your request).
      Sign-in works without cookies: the session token is stored exclusively locally in your browser
      (localStorage). You can permanently delete your account yourself at any time in the
      <a href="/account.html">account dashboard</a> — this irreversibly removes all associated
      data (profile, favorites, tool data, credentials).
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Processor: Supabase, Inc.; data residency in the EU (AWS eu-central-1, Frankfurt). For details
      on how the service processes data, see
      <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" rel="noopener">supabase.com/privacy</a>.
      A connection to Supabase is only established when you use account features
      (registration, sign-in, favorites, account-bound tools) — not when merely browsing the site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="support">Voluntary support (Stripe, PayPal)</h2>
    <p>
      On the <a href="/support.html">Support</a> page you can voluntarily contribute towards the
      running costs of this project. Nothing on this site is behind a paywall, and a contribution
      buys no goods, services or account privileges.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Stripe.</strong> When you press the button, this website asks Stripe to create a
      payment page and then sends you there. Everything you enter — payment method, card details,
      billing data, e-mail address — you enter <em>on Stripe’s page</em>, not on this one. This
      website never receives, sees or stores your payment details. Stripe processes the payment on
      its own responsibility as an independent controller under its own privacy policy.
      The legal basis for the transfer that starts the process is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR (carrying out
      the payment you initiated).
    </p>
    <p>
      Once a payment has been confirmed, Stripe notifies this project’s server component. What is
      stored on our side is deliberately reduced to what a running total needs: <strong>the amount,
      the currency, the time, and Stripe’s technical reference numbers for the transaction</strong>.
      <strong>No name, no e-mail address, no address and no payment details are stored by us</strong>,
      and the stored records are not publicly readable. The figure shown publicly on the Support page
      is the sum alone. The address you are returned to afterwards carries no amount either — it
      only says that you came back.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Payment service provider: Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd. (Ireland), with onward transfer to
      Stripe, Inc. (USA). For details on how the service processes data, see
      <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">stripe.com/privacy</a>. A connection to
      Stripe is only established when you press the button — not when merely reading the page.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>PayPal.</strong> As a second route the Support page carries an ordinary link to
      PayPal.me. It is a link and nothing more: no PayPal script runs on this site, and no data is
      transmitted until you follow it. From that point PayPal’s own privacy policy applies
      (<a href="https://www.paypal.com/webapps/mpp/ua/privacy-full" rel="noopener">paypal.com</a>).
      This route reports nothing back to us, so payments made through it are not recorded
      automatically anywhere on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Fonts</h2>
    <p>All web fonts are served locally by this website. No connection to Google Fonts is made.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      You have the rights under Art. 15–21 GDPR (access, rectification, erasure, restriction, data
      portability, objection) and the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority
      (Art. 77 GDPR). Without a user account, this website does not collect or store personal data
      about you; with an account, you can view, change and fully delete your data yourself in the
      dashboard at any time — if in doubt, reach out by e-mail.
    </p>
  </div>
</main>
<Attribution sources={[]} />
</Layout>
